From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] hdd: return the actual management TX submission error

The caller currently reports success even if the P2P submission returned an
error. wlan_cfg80211_mgmt_tx already returns a Linux errno, so preserve the
int result without converting it a second time from QDF_STATUS. This is a
diagnostic fix, not an AWDL injection implementation. Apply only to the pinned
WLAN source and validate in the isolated build first.

diff --git a/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_p2p.c b/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_p2p.c
--- a/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_p2p.c
+++ b/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_p2p.c
@@ -281,7 +281,7 @@ static int __wlan_hdd_mgmt_tx(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct wireless_dev *wdev,
 			      const u8 *buf, size_t len, bool no_cck,
 			      bool dont_wait_for_ack, u64 *cookie)
 {
-	QDF_STATUS status;
+	int status;
 	struct net_device *dev = wdev->netdev;
 	struct hdd_adapter *adapter = WLAN_HDD_GET_PRIV_PTR(dev);
 	struct hdd_context *hdd_ctx = WLAN_HDD_GET_CTX(adapter);
@@ -360,7 +360,7 @@ off_chan_tx:
 		  chan ? chan->center_freq : 0, wait, offchan,
 		  dont_wait_for_ack, status, *cookie);
 
-	return 0;
+	return status;
 }
 
 #if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 14, 0))
